abstract: "A reusable quantitative analysis framework based on Theodore Paul Wright's Wright's Law (1936), Learning Curve theory, and the Boston Consulting Group's Experience Curve extension. Designed to assist in manufacturing cost forecasting, technology cost prediction, and economies of scale analysis. Includes tools for estimating learning rates from historical production data, predicting cost trajectories, and evaluating competitiveness through the market-share-to-cost-advantage logic chain. This skill provides a quantitative framework and writing style calibration, and does NOT claim to represent Wright personally or his unpublished views. Wright passed away in 1970; all subsequent validations (solar PV, lithium-ion batteries, etc.) are the work of later researchers."
